  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Hard freeze coming for the mornings.\n\n- Valley fog and stratus will be common early this week.\n\n- A warming and drying trend this week.\n\n- Another cold and cold front on the way for early next week.\n\nThe winter storm is winding down this morning as the upper level\nlow over the Pacific northwest is migrating south today. Expect\ncool, cloudy weather today as both the moisture source and the\nsource of the cold air are cut off from the region today. That\nbeing said, there's quite a bit of cold air already in our area\nfrom this storm.  \n\nDue to the cold air mass in place, increasing stability, and a\ndrier air mass aloft moving, expect some very cold, foggy mornings\nahead. The next few mornings will be a battle between how much it\ncan cool off at night, and how much fog and stratus can form in\nthe valleys to keep things warmer. In any case, there's plenty of\npotential for a hard freeze the next few mornings with\ntemperatures in the low to mid 20s for much of western Montana.\nHowever, due to the recent moisture, as it gets cold at night that\nwill be limited by fog formation. If the fog forms, temperatures\nin the mid to upper 20s are more likely in the mornings, but if\nthere are breaks in the fog, especially in the high elevation\nvalleys, then it will get quite cold quickly. \n\nThrough the week a ridge will build back in over the region. This\nwill cause more stable conditions, limiting how quickly fog can\nburn off in western Montana. Central Idaho and far northwest\nMontana picked up far less moisture from this recent storm, so\nthat will be less of an impact there. However, the building ridge\nwill cause temperatures to rise to above average for this time of\nyear by the end of the week. \n\nEnsembles are starting to agree on another cold front for early\nnext week, so the warmer, drier weather at the end of the week\nwill only last a few days. So far ensembles are showing less\npotential for moisture with the next front, especially if it comes\nthrough as an open wave vs a closed low like this last one. So it\nwont' be a repeat of this system, but will probably come with more\nwesterly winds, some precipitation, and a good cool down.",
